{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>and the Amalekite.</b> Some ask: were they dwelling in the valley? But it is written immediately afterward: ״וירד העמלקי והכנעני היושב בהר״. Rather, thus said the Holy One, blessed be He: this is a deep stratagem — that they should turn toward the way of the wilderness and not fight, for they would not succeed, even though they are wicked, for He does not rejoice in their downfall. And according to the plain sense, they are indeed dwelling in the valley, but when they heard that Israel were coming against them by way of the Atharim, they went up into the mountain and lay in ambush for them — and in the context of an ambush the expression of dwelling is apt, as it is written: ״ישב במארב חצרים״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:27.977723303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}